.TH POSTUREFLOW 1 "September 2026" "postureflow 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
postureflow \- Context-aware security, developer, and lifestyle profile manager for Pop!_OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B postureflow
[\fB\-\-home\fR | \fB\-\-work\fR | \fB\-\-dev\fR | \fB\-\-travel\fR | \fB\-\-secure\fR]
.br
.B postureflow
[\fB\-i\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR | \fB\-\-score\fR | \fB\-\-ports\fR | \fB\-\-autoflow\fR]
.br
.B postureflow
[\fB\-\-evil\-twin\-check\fR | \fB\-\-cloak\-status\fR | \fB\-\-uncloak\fR | \fB\-\-dns\-status\fR]
.br
.B postureflow
[\fB\-\-test\fR]
.br
.B postureflow
[\fB\-r\fR | \fB\-\-reset\fR | \fB\-\-default\fR]
.br
.B postureflow
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B postureflow
is a lifestyle- and security-aware system profile manager tailored for Pop!_OS. It dynamically reconfigures the Netfilter firewall (\fBufw\fR), Linux kernel parameters (\fBsysctl\fR), PAM resource limits, and desktop session idle-locks according to four distinct operational contexts:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHOME\fR: Casual browsing, video streaming, Steam/Proton gaming, and local device synchronization.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWORK\fR: Corporate office and VPN connectivity, network printer discovery, while strictly preventing development test servers from leaking onto company subnets.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEV\fR: Software engineering and debugging; attaches debuggers without friction, scales inotify watcher tables to 524k, and enables core dump analysis.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTRAVEL\fR: Hostile/untrusted network lockdown (coffee shops, airports, hotel Wi-Fi) with maximum stealth, Anti-Evil Twin Wi-Fi fingerprinting, and Anti-DNS-Leak egress protection.

.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B \-\-home
.B Casual, Media Streaming & Gaming Mode
.br
Sets \fBvm.max_map_count = 1048576\fR for Proton gaming, allows Steam Remote Play & peer-to-peer LAN downloads (ports 27031\(en27040), GSConnect/KDE Connect phone pairing (ports 1714\(en1764), LocalSend file sharing (port 53317), Chromecast mDNS (port 5353 UDP), and relaxes screen lock timeout to 30 minutes.

.TP
.B \-\-work
.B Office, Corporate VPN & Compliance Mode
.br
Unblocks corporate VPN tunnel adapters (\fBwg+\fR, \fBtun+\fR, \fBtap+\fR, \fBtailscale+\fR), opens CUPS printing and mDNS, strictly blocks development ports (3000, 8000...) from the office LAN, and enforces a 5-minute compliance screen lock.

.TP
.B \-\-dev
.B Active Engineering & Debugging Mode
.br
Configures \fBkernel.yama.ptrace_scope = 1\fR for debuggers (gdb, lldb, VS Code), scales \fBfs.inotify.max_user_watches = 524288\fR for Vite/Webpack, enables core dumps for crash analysis, opens local web dev and container bridge ports, and automatically uncloaks developer credentials.

.TP
.B \-t\fR, \fB\-\-travel\fR, \fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-secure
.B Hardened Travel & Public Wi-Fi Mode
.br
Paranoid lockdown: closes all inbound ports, drops outbound plaintext DNS queries (port 53 UDP/TCP) to prevent tracking, sets \fBkernel.yama.ptrace_scope = 2\fR against memory scraping, disables crash dumps, enforces anti-spoofing and SYN cookie protections, and sets a 5-minute screen lock. (\fB\-\-secure\fR is retained as a backwards-compatible alias).

.TP
.B \-\-evil\-twin\-check
.B Anti-Evil Twin Wi-Fi Verification
.br
Scans active Wi-Fi BSSID and default gateway MAC address against configured trusted network fingerprints to detect rogue access points.

.TP
.B \-\-cloak\-status
.B Developer Credential Cloaking Report
.br
Inspects filesystem permissions on \fB~/.aws/credentials\fR, memory-resident identities in \fBssh-agent\fR, and password manager CLI lock states.

.TP
.B \-\-uncloak
.B Developer Credential Uncloaking
.br
Restores read/write permissions (\fB0600\fR) on \fB~/.aws/credentials\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-dns\-status
.B Encrypted DNS & Anti-DNS-Leak Status
.br
Displays active DNS-over-TLS (DoT) encryption status, DNSSEC validation, and UFW Anti-DNS-Leak outbound drop rules.

.TP
.B \-\-reset\fR, \fB\-\-default
.B Pop!_OS Factory Default Mode
.br
Restores the system to official Pop!_OS out-of-the-box defaults: disables and resets UFW firewall, removes custom sysctl and limits configurations, restores standard kernel parameters, sets desktop idle screen lock to 15 minutes, restores platform power profile to 'balanced', and resets battery charge thresholds to 100%.

.SH ANTI-LOCKOUT GUARANTEES
.B postureflow
includes built-in invariant safeguards:
.IP 1. 4
\fBSSH Auto-Preservation\fR: Port 22/tcp is automatically whitelisted if an active SSH connection or listening daemon is detected.
.IP 2. 4
\fBLoopback IPC Guarantee\fR: Traffic on \fBlo\fR is permanently allowed, ensuring desktop environments, audio, and D-Bus never freeze.
.IP 3. 4
\fBUnrestricted Outbound Traffic\fR: Default-allow outgoing policy ensures web browsing, DNS, and package updates never fail.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/postureflow-state
Active profile tracker.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/99-postureflow.conf
Dynamic kernel parameter drop-in.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99-postureflow-health
Automated post-upgrade health hook.

